      "additions": 2,
      "blob_url": "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/blob/1138678bca887d4e6d05db38d3f89e6b3e119a60/docs%2Fcontributing%2Fmodel%2Ftranscription.md",
      "changes": 3,
      "contents_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/vllm-project/vllm/contents/docs%2Fcontributing%2Fmodel%2Ftranscription.md?ref=1138678bca887d4e6d05db38d3f89e6b3e119a60",
      "deletions": 1,
      "filename": "docs/contributing/model/transcription.md",
      "patch": "@@ -195,7 +195,8 @@ Provide a fast duration→token estimate to improve streaming usage statistics:\n The API server takes care of basic audio I/O and optional chunking before building prompts:\n \n - Resampling: Input audio is resampled to `SpeechToTextConfig.sample_rate` using `AudioResampler`.\n-- Chunking: If `SpeechToTextConfig.allow_audio_chunking` is True and the duration exceeds `max_audio_clip_s`, the server splits the audio into overlapping chunks and generates a prompt per chunk. Overlap is controlled by `overlap_chunk_second`.\n+- Chunking: If `SpeechToTextConfig.allow_audio_chunking` is True and the duration exceeds `max_audio_clip_s`, the server splits audio into contiguous chunks and generates a prompt per chunk.\n+- Split-window search: `overlap_chunk_second` defines a search window near each nominal boundary where the server picks a low-energy split point. This shifts chunk boundaries but does not create duplicated overlap in output chunks.\n - Energy-aware splitting: When `min_energy_split_window_size` is set, the server finds low-energy regions to minimize cutting within words.\n \n Relevant server logic:",
      "raw_url": "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/raw/1138678bca887d4e6d05db38d3f89e6b3e119a60/docs%2Fcontributing%2Fmodel%2Ftranscription.md",
      "sha": "0fbd9742ea9c7a30aace85fb8fbb8e0e016aa450",
      "status": "modified"
    },
    {
      "additions": 8,
      "blob_url": "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/blob/1138678bca887d4e6d05db38d3f89e6b3e119a60/tests%2Fentrypoints%2Fspeech_to_text%2Ftest_speech_to_text_cancellation.py",
      "changes": 10,
